 "response": {
  "text": "If your main concern is **active pimples, blackheads, or clogged pores**, I’d buy a **2% salicylic-acid serum** rather than a generic brightening serum. Current Indian listings put several good options well below ₹700. [www.nykaa.com](https://www.nykaa.com/dp/serum-for-open-pores?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### My picks\n\n### [Minimalist Salicylic Acid Face Serum]()\n*₹494*\n\n**Best overall: Minimalist 2% Salicylic Acid** — around ₹494 currently. Good choice for oily/acne-prone skin, particularly blackheads and clogged pores. [www.1mg.com](https://www.1mg.com/categories/skin-care/face-serums-4432?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### [The Derma Co Sali-Cinamide Anti-Acne Serum]()\n*₹527*\n\n### [Chemist At Play 2% Salicylic Acid Face Serum]()\n*₹255*\n\n### [Foxtale 12% Niacinamide + Azelaic Acid Serum]()\n*₹187*\n\n### [Minimalist Niacinamide Face Serum]()\n*₹212*\n\n- **For active acne:** The Derma Co Sali-Cinamide — 2% salicylic acid + 5% niacinamide.\n- **For a cheaper salicylic option:** Chemist At Play 2% Salicylic Acid.\n- **For acne + leftover dark marks:** Foxtale's niacinamide + azelaic-acid formula.\n- **For sensitive skin/oil control rather than frequent breakouts:** a lower-strength niacinamide serum may be gentler.\n\n**How I'd use it:** start the salicylic serum **2–3 nights per week**, then increase if your skin tolerates it. Don't stack it initially with retinol, other exfoliating acids, or harsh scrubs. Use sunscreen every morning.\n\nIf you tell me whether your skin is **oily, dry, combination, or sensitive** and whether you have **active pimples vs acne marks**, I can narrow it down to one.",
